      ":question/problem": "Express $3\\log_{5}(198) - 3\\log_{5}(18)$ as a single logarithm.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n(a)-\\log_n(b)=\\log_n\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\log_{5}(198)-3\\log_{5}(18)&=3\\bigl(\\log_{5}(198)-\\log_{5}(18)\\bigr) \\\\ &=3\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{198}{18}\\right) \\\\ &=3\\log_{5}(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n3\\log_{5}(198)-3\\log_{5}(18)=3\\log_{5}(11)\n$$",
